# FEATURE-FACTS (G3)

[compose_flip.rs]
Place: symbol `bridges` (the `let bridges: Arc<dyn crate::compose_mcp::BridgeFeatures> = ...` line, after `late_computer_hosts`). Replace the ToolBridges construction with:

    let bridges: Arc<dyn crate::compose_mcp::BridgeFeatures> = Arc::new(crate::mcp_surface::ToolBridges {
        host: b.host.clone(),
        desktop: { let config = config.clone(); Arc::new(move || config.desktop_settings()) },
        computer: late_computer_hosts.clone(),
    });

`config` must be the Arc<Config> in scope at that point (if it is built later than this line, move the `bridges` line after it; no other reader of `bridges` precedes it).
ToolBridges no longer holds `files`/SharedBridgeFiles. `bridge_files` (BridgeFiles::new, `.sink()` in the FanOutSink, `.start(core_watcher)`) keeps being built and started by the golden bridge.json loading; nothing in production reads its `present` any more. The lead decides whether to keep that watch until the Node runtime is retired (x-del-bridge-servers).

SERVICE_PENDING: nothing to remove.
Cargo: no new dependency edge (mixdog-core-api, mixdog-core-config are already dependencies of mixdog-app-server-daemon).

# Not done: method-level claim check
`HostChannel::serves(capability)` (mixdog-core-api host.rs, Outgoing in mixdog-app-server outgoing.rs) answers per capability only (`claimant(capability, None)`).
"browser absent when the claimant does not serve host/browser/command" needs `fn serves_method(&self, capability: HostCapability, method: Method) -> bool` (default `self.serves(capability)`) on HostChannel (hot file host.rs) and an override in Outgoing = `self.claimant(capability, Some(method)).is_ok()`; then `ToolBridges::present` passes `|c| host.serves_method(c, <host/browser/command|host/visualize/command|host/computer/*>)`. Until then a claimant that declared the capability but listed other methods counts as serving it.
